on and  ad partner click counts that we already  had defined in our original feature  service  so this is the data set that we can uh  use to train our model off of but uh  let's also see how we can get this data  online so that we ultimately can do uh  real-time inference and to do that let's  go back to my cli here  and  hit that rest api endpoint for our new  feature service here this v2 service and  we'll ask for a particular user id and  add partner id so this is the case where  we have an ad that we could show to a  user and we want to get back a feature  vector that we can pass to our model  that will ultimately predict if the user  will click on that ad  and what we can see is techton responds  back at low latency with that  latest set of online feature values that  we can use to make our predictions  and so there you have it in just a short  amount of time we were able to  connect a new data source from our  snowflake account uh just define some  features against it register that and  make it available to my whole  organization to discover and reuse then  we were able to extend our existing  feature set for our ad prediction model  with our new with our new feature view  here and ultimately get that data  offline for training and then online for  serving for our model  so i hope you enjoyed this demo and  thanks for watching  just to sum it all up basically what  you've now seen is how techton and  snowflake together really provide you  with a full feature platform that solves  the data problems around machine  learning we've got snowflake at the core  layer the source of truth for all your  raw data and use tecton to manage your  ml features and to serve those ml  features for training and serving  purposes and then finally the only thing  you now really need to  train and deploy ml models is a data  science environment like sagemaker or  jupiter or whatever your data science  environment of choice is to be up and  running and build and deploy real-time  m